readings.c3s2:
¶

'''II.''' ''a.'' Noting a position in which a valve-view is presented; valval.

'''valviferous''' (val-vif′e̤-rus), ''a.'' [< L. ''valva'', valve, + ''ferre'' = E. ''bear''<sup>1</sup>.] Bearing a valve; provided with a valve or valvular parts.

'''valviform''' (val′vi-fôrm), ''a.'' [< L. ''valva'', the leaf of a door (see ''valve''), + ''forma'', form.] Forming or acting as a valve; valvular; valvate. Also ''valvæform.''

'''valvula''' (val′vū-lä̤), ''n.''; pl. ''valvulæ'' (-lē). [NL.: see ''valvule.''] In ''anat.'', same as ''valve.''—{{smaller|'''Valvula Bauhini''', the ileocæcal valve.—'''Valvulæ conniventes''', transverse folds of the mucous membrane and underlying tissues found throughout a large extent of the small intestine. Their use is probably to retard somewhat the passage of the alimentary mass, and at the same time to offer a greater surface for absorption.—'''Valvula Heisteri''', folds of the mucous membrane, in the neck of the gall-bladder and in the cystic duct, which present the appearance of a spiral valve. See cut under ''stomach.''—'''Valvula Vieussensii''', the valve of Vieussens (which see, under ''valve'').}}

'''valvular''' (val′vū-lär), ''a.'' [< ''valvule'' + ''-ar''<sup>3</sup>.] Of or pertaining to a valve or valvula; also, having the character of a valve; valviform.—{{smaller|'''Valvular disease''', disease of one or more of the valves of the heart.—'''Valvular sinus.''' See ''sinus.''}}

'''valvule''' (val′vūl), ''n.'' [< F. ''valvule''; < L. ''valvola'', ''valvula'', dim. of ''valva'', the leaf of a door, etc.: see ''valve.''] '''1.''' A little valve. {{smaller|Specifically—(''a'') In ''anat.'': (1) The valvula or valve of Vieussens. (2) One of the valvulæ conniventes. (''b'') In ''bot.'', a name formerly given to the inner or flowering glumes of grasses. (''c'') In ''entom.'', a corneous piece at the base of the haustellum of sucking insects, corresponding to the labrum in the mandibulate mouth. ''Kirby and Spence.''—'''Interventricular valvules.''' See ''interventricular.''}}
